  ("How do you count contractions in a base?", "Measure each pullback from its local high to its local low as a percentage. A base going 18%, then 9%, then 4.5% is a three-contraction base, usually written 3T. Two to four contractions is normal; if you are counting six, you are almost certainly drawing what you want to see."),
